🐛 Bug
compute_inline is a transformation that tries to replace a load from a buffer with its defining expression. In order to find this expression, it scans the TE statement looking for stores to that buffer - it expects to find a single store with simple indices. Simple indices here means that they are just Vars and not compound expressions (this is needed so that we can figure out to correctly rewrite the load).
The problem arises when some of the dimensions of the buffer have size 1 and the statement has been simplified: in this case indices that previously were Vars could be rewritten with 0. In this case we still can unambiguously recreate the expression for the inlined buffer, so we should do it.
