Problem Description
IRSimplifier should be able to reason about value ranges of variables to simplify mod statements.
For instance, in the following statement
{
  for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++) {
    B[i] = A[i % 100];
  }
}

i % 100 can be replaced with i since i is always less than 100 (it's a loop variable that iterates from 0 to 100).
However, IRSimplifier doesn't do that now.
